<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-5452] GridTimeoutProcessor can hang on stop.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-5452</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;PFA repro attached.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Actually, there are 2 issue.&lt;br/&gt;
1. GridTimeoutProcessor can&apos;t be stopped if TimeoutObject eats InterruptedException. We should handle this correctly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2. TX use TimeoutObjects to be rolled back by timeout.  However, TXs doesn&apos;t remove their TimeoutObjects on node stop. &lt;br/&gt;
Possible, TimeoutObject doesn&apos;t removed on TX rollback and this should be investigated.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
